## 3. Known defects in the export — the importer must be defensive

These are real, observed in the reference file. Handle them; do not assume a clean input.

| Defect | Evidence | Required behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| **Dangling links** | 4 same-module out-links point at absolute numbers 445, 446, 367, 374, which are absent. The DXL skips deleted *objects* but only filters deleted *modules*, so links to deleted objects survive. | Create `__UNDEFINED` placeholders (R5). Count and report. |
| **Corrupt metadata key** | Object `SRD-1023` has `__taSbleRowIndex` instead of `__tableRowIndex`. | Detect unknown `__`-prefixed keys, log a warning, keep the value under its literal key. Never crash. |
| **Missing `\r` escaping** | The DXL escapes `\`, `\n`, `"`, `\t` (in the correct order) but not CR or other C0 controls. A CR in DOORS text emits a raw control character → invalid JSON. | Parse strictly. On `JSONDecodeError`, report the byte offset and surrounding text so the user can locate the offending object. Do not attempt silent repair. |
| **Unescaped attribute *names*** | Only values are escaped. A DOORS attribute name containing `"` or `\` corrupts the file. | Same as above. |
| **Duplicate JSON keys** | User attributes are emitted *after* `id` / `objectNumber` / `objectLevel`. A module defining a visible attribute literally named `id` yields a duplicate key; most parsers silently keep the last, destroying the metadata. | Parse with a duplicate-key detecting hook (`object_pairs_hook`). On collision: keep the **metadata** value, store the DOORS attribute under `attr::<name>`, and emit an ERROR-level report entry. |
| **Hard object cap** | `getModuleContents(url, 0, 12000)` is hardcoded. Modules over 12 000 objects truncate **silently**. | If `len(__contents) >= 12000`, emit a prominent warning that the export is probably truncated. |
| **Scrubbed reference file** | Every user attribute in the supplied example is `""`, including `Object Type` and `Absolute Number`. | The importer must work with empty attributes throughout. Empty `Object Type` → `DOORSTBD` (§5.1). Empty `Absolute Number` → store as absent, warn once per module. |

Also note, for context only: the DXL declares `__system`, `__instanceOf`, `__sourceType`,
`__moduleType`, `__releaseNr` and `OBJECT_NAME_ATTR_NAME` but never emits them. Do not
expect these fields.

