## 9. Implementation notes

**Stack:** Python 3.14+, official `neo4j` driver, CLI entry point. Change if you have a
reason, but keep the parse/derive logic pure and unit-testable, separate from the driver
code.

**Structure the derivation rules as isolated pure functions** — `target_object_url`,
`parent_number`, `sort_key`, `derive_name`, `derive_labels`, `derive_id`. These are where
every subtle rule lives and where the unit tests go. A future change to the identity
scheme should touch `derive_id` and nothing else.

**CLI:**

```
import <file.json> [--uri] [--user] [--database neo4j] [--batch-size 1000]
                   [--dry-run] [--report out.json]
init-schema
validate
```

`--dry-run` performs Phase 0 and all derivation, writes the report, touches nothing.

