## 10. Extension points — leave the seams, build nothing

- **Baseline ↔ current comparison.** Baseline and current imports produce disjoint
  subgraphs with no relationship between them, because their URLs differ. A future
  `__versionOf` / `__supersedes` edge is the intended mechanism.
- **Link semantics.** The DXL discards the DOORS link-module name, so all links are
  untyped `refersTo`. Recovering satisfies/verifies/refines requires extending the DXL to
  emit the link module name — a change to the exporter, not the importer. This will
  matter for real traceability analysis; flag it to the user.
- **Non-DOORS sources.** They join on `SEItem` and must supply `__id`, `__name`,
  `__version`. They will not have `__objectUrl`.
- **Deriving `Absolute Number`.** Deliberately not done — it is read from the attribute
  per the agreed rule. The URL does encode it, which makes a cheap consistency check
  possible later if the data ever warrants it.

